# L0: Codex findings whose quoted ranges are not co-located with any primary/replica record (never in a multi-run region).
# Each is normalized to the claim it attributes to the quoted text; all remain singletons (NO_CO_LOCATED_RECORD_FROM_OTHER_RUN).
CX X:BF-L0-0013 | The technology-neutral runtime rule file loads only for backend C# paths (reported: frontend runtime work lacks automatic coverage).
CX X:BF-L0-0014 | The security rule file's path globs omit standalone scripts and unlisted configuration formats (reported trigger gap).
CX X:BF-L0-0016 | Automatic test-rule loading depends on Tests naming, .spec.ts files or an e2e folder (reported trigger gap).
CX X:BF-L0-0037 | Shell tokenization in the pre-bash hook does not distinguish comments or heredoc content from executable commands (reported false positives).
CX X:BF-L0-0038 | Nested-shell parsing is depth-limited and does not inspect script or encoded-command contents (reported: indirect overrides escape the guard).
CX X:BF-L0-0040 | Git manifest discovery excludes ignored files and the unborn-branch baseline treats existing manifests as unchanged (reported missing delta reminder).
CX X:BF-L0-0043 | Co-change detection uses regexes that assume exact project and directory names (reported missed seeder reminders).
CX X:BF-L0-0044 | The Stop-hook digest includes only the first 500 sorted relevant files (reported missed re-reminders).
CX X:BF-L0-0048 | The manifest check infers project roles from names and reads MSBuild XML without evaluation (reported accuracy limits for conditional and property-expanded references).
CX X:BF-L0-0049 | Central Package Management is recognized only as a literal unqualified switch in the inspected file (reported false 'missing CPM' for imported settings).
CX X:BF-L0-0053 | npm delta extraction omits optionalDependencies and collapses repeated section declarations by package ID (reported missed deltas).
CX X:BF-L0-0062 | The error-handling example maps request cancellation to status 499 (reported as a status choice beyond the cancellation rule).
CX X:BF-L0-0078 | The EF Core mapping example embeds a monetary precision and an index without a local product-approval caveat (reported copy risk).
CX X:BF-L0-0092 | The Serilog bootstrap example logs a fatal startup failure without rethrowing or setting a failure exit status (reported failure-visibility uncertainty).
CX X:BF-L0-0095 | The C# property example trims and rejects whitespace silently (reported copy risk for unapproved string semantics).
